From 3dfd97522f589907bbe03a99162fe9a2ef5c603e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E7=94=B0=E5=AE=81?= <tianning24@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:32:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: Add RVV wcschrnul with multiarch wiring
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add an RVV wcschrnul implementation and wire it into the RISC-V
multiarch IFUNC machinery.  Select it when hwprobe reports the V
extension, and retain the generic implementation as the fallback.

Probe positions 0 through 4 with straight-line scalar loads before
entering the e32, LMUL=8 vector loop.  This avoids vector startup and
loop-control costs for the small inputs which regressed on both tested
microarchitectures.  The vector loop uses fault-only-first loads and
returns the first element which either matches the requested wide
character or is a terminating wide NUL.

Performance was measured from official upstream commit
d5bd0f22305277fa0d431bb9d733aa9456706573.  bench-wcschrnul was pinned
to CPU 2, warmed once, and run six times.  The vector and generic
implementations were measured in the same process.  Each result below
uses the median timing for each case followed by the geometric mean of
the vector/generic ratios.  Positive values are time reductions.

Scan position  Cases   K3 X100   32-core RVV target
0-4               30     14.82%              36.78%
5-16              76    -20.52%              16.43%
17-64            149     41.19%              52.32%
65-256           125     58.80%              57.98%
>256             100     61.37%              46.72%
All               480     43.69%              47.48%

The previous vector-only implementation regressed by 98.16% on K3 and
29.41% on the 32-core target for positions 0 through 4.  The scalar
prologue removes that regression on both systems.  On K3 it retains a
20.52% regression for positions 5 through 16; this tradeoff is recorded
rather than hidden by a platform-specific threshold.

Validation on both systems:
- make test t=wcsmbs/test-wcschrnul: PASS
- bench-wcschrnul coverage: 480/480 cases in all six formal runs

Signed-off-by: 田宁 <tianning24@iscas.ac.cn>
